    "category": "network",
    "description": "Since early this morning the customer API service has been unreliable under normal load: a portion of client requests are refused outright while others connect and then drop mid-request, and the service intermittently stops responding for a few seconds at a time before recovering. Customers report sporadic errors and timeouts on the API; the customer web service is unaffected. This is a P1 customer-impacting incident.\nThe overnight on-call suspects the API backend pool is simply under-provisioned, or that one of the pool members has gone bad, and is asking whether we should add more capacity/hardware to the pool or pull and replace the suspect member.\nInvestigate across the available systems, confirm the actual root cause before you change anything, restore the API service to reliable operation under normal load, leave every system in a correct and consistent state, and resolve this incident once the service is healthy again.",
